---
# Reserve the tail of the boot disk for LVMS.
#
# Do NOT try to size partition 4 here. Ignition honours that directive, but
# ignition-ostree-growfs runs immediately afterwards and growpart expands root
# into any free space that follows it, undoing the resize. Measured on the NUC's
# first boot: Ignition set partition 4 to 419430400 sectors (200 GiB), and one
# second later growfs logged
#   CHANGED: partition=4 old: size=419430400 new: size=1999358607
#
# Declaring a partition AFTER root is what actually pins it. At ignition-disks
# time root is still the image's ~4 GiB, so there is room to create partition 5;
# growpart can then only grow root up to partition 5's start. With no free space
# left, growpart reports NOCHANGE, which cannot fail the boot because the service
# invokes it as `growpart "${PKNAME}" "${partnum}" || :`.
#
# sizeMiB is deliberately omitted so the partition extends to the end of the
# disk. It is left unformatted and unmounted: LVMS auto-discovery claims unused
# partitions, so playbooks/install_lvms.yml needs no deviceSelector. The label
# only has to avoid the reserved bios/boot/reserved names that LVMS filters out.
apiVersion: machineconfiguration.openshift.io/v1
kind: MachineConfig
metadata:
  labels:
    machineconfiguration.openshift.io/role: master
  name: 98-lvms-partition
spec:
  config:
    ignition:
      version: 3.2.0
    storage:
      disks:
        - device: {{ sno_disk_device }}
          partitions:
            - label: lvms
              number: 5
              startMiB: {{ sno_root_partition_size_gb | int * 1024 }}
              wipePartitionEntry: true
